<td id="S6.T3.6.1.5.13" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T3.6.1.5.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.65</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE IV</span>: </span><span id="S6.T4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Obstacle avoidance performance in 4-DoF in Hills and Pillars scenarios with varying terrain.<span id="S6.T4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We evaluate DUViN-air and DUViN in obstacle avoidance tasks under two environments with continuously varying terrain height: </span>Hills<span id="S6.T4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> and </span>Pillars<span id="S6.T4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. DUViN exhibits more robust performance under increasing turbidity, demonstrating improved adaptability to complex underwater environments.</span></span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
